From 09583529d55733b7ac3060697e41ac51da89bd51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:38:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): resume a session on its owning gateway, and
 follow the owner on 4007 [daveey]

With several registry gateways in one sidebar, a resume whose owner could not
be proven at that instant fell through to the selected gateway. The owner
record was fragile: a resume routed by a connection-tagged unified-list row
never persisted an owner hint, so navigation opens (route change, session
switcher, step keys) left nothing behind. Once the owning gateway's rows left
the unified list (its pooled backend reconnecting; only pooled gateways are
read), the next route re-resume probed only the selected gateway's store and
sent session.resume there. Older backends then fabricated an empty session,
so the chat opened empty and the selected gateway never moved.

- persist the tagged row's owner as the hint when none is recorded
- before dispatching an owner-less resume the selected store cannot find,
  look the id up across connections (unified rows, hints, by-id probe of the
  other registry connections) and resume there
- on JSON-RPC 4007 from the dispatched gateway, follow the owner the same
  way (pinning it as the only hint) instead of running not-found handling;
  each connection is tried at most once per open
- single-gateway installs never probe and behave as before
